# `var opts = options || {}`: at the join the function's own empty literal (L0, proven on its way in) meets what was seen to arrive as `options` (L2, the caller's literal). No family holds
# L0 and L2, so the expectation L0|L2 had no test ("EXPECTED HAS NO TEST") and all eight reads off `opts` went by name, whether options were given or not. Now the members that answer one of
# the names used off the value are asked first (L2: the reads are slots), and on the failing side the silent ones by their shapes (L0: every read is undefined). f1 = configure.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = NewObject layout=L0
# CHECK: = ShapeTest {{*}}layouts=[L2] [rejectsMarkedObjects]
# CHECK: = GetSlot {{*}}key="encoding" receivers=[L2] level=Proven
# CHECK: = ShapeTest {{*}}layouts=[L0] [rejectsMarkedObjects]
# CHECK: = GetSlot {{*}}key="limit" receivers=[L2] level=Proven
# CHECK: = ShapeTest {{*}}layouts=[L0] [rejectsMarkedObjects]
# -- source: the-own-empty-literal-and-a-layout-seen-to-arrive-are-asked-in-two-turns.cjs
